{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"POST-REMEDIATION FIVE-RUN DISTRIBUTION (2026-08-14/15): successful full-route runs 31846417650, 31848073556, 31850293962, 31851563349, and 31851589360 were created after merged cancellation/static-Pandoc changes and all contain the macOS job. End-to-end durations were 1787, 1807, 2071, 1899, and 1880s: N=5 mean 1888.8s = 31m28.8s, median 1880s = 31m20s. Thus actual time-to-completed-vote remains 88.8s above the 30m average target. The last required non-vote job was macOS in every run; creation-to-mac-complete averaged 1813.4s = 30m13.4s (median 1773s = 29m33s). macOS job execution itself averaged 1676.2s = 27m56.2s (median 1686s = 28m06s). The gap is orchestration: admission/routing before macOS plus final vote dispatch. Final-vote wait after macOS completion was 3, 3, 70, 146, and 107s (mean 65.8s, median 70s); vote execution averaged 8.8s. Latest merged conftest run 31851589360 completed substantive gates in 29m22s and the workflow in 31m20s, with 1m46s of final-vote runner queue. Conclusion: the critical-path test job is inside 20-30m on average, but the end-to-end goal is not yet met. A coverage-neutral macOS reduction of roughly 90s would cover current orchestration variance; repeated store-fixture construction remains the active consensus-backed lever. Do not claim target achieved until a later full-route average is <=1800s."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786753939331748001,"uuid":"07bd5c00-77ea-4af0-a07c-a7af447b8674"}